-- title:
--   Drinfeld deformation ring has a point over any complete √q-algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and write $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ for $W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$. Let $O^{nr}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain which is a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra, complete and separated for the ideal generated by the image of $q$, that ideal being maximal, and with algebraically closed residue field $k$; let $\iota:\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}\to O^{nr}$ be a ring homomorphism and $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $k$ (a commutative two-dimensional formal group law with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ by law endomorphisms and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[q]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[\mathrm{Frob}\,a]\circ\varpi$) which is special for $\mathrm{res}\circ\iota$, i.e. its Lie algebra is the direct sum of the two invertible pieces $\mathrm{lieZero}$ and $\mathrm{lieOne}$, and has height $4$. Let $R$ be a noetherian local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete and separated for its maximal ideal, $\mathrm{res}_R:R\to k$ compatible with the structure map, $X_u$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $R$ and $w_u$ an isomorphism from $X_u\otimes_{\mathrm{res}_R}k$ to $X_0$. Assume $(R,\mathrm{res}_R,X_u,w_u)$ pro-represents deformations of $X_0$: for every Artinian local $O^{nr}$-algebra $A$ with surjective compatible $\mathrm{res}_A:A\to k$, every special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ over $A$ of height $4$ and every isomorphism $w:X\otimes_{\mathrm{res}_A}k\to X_0$, there is a unique $O^{nr}$-algebra map $\chi:R\to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\chi=\mathrm{res}_R$ admitting an isomorphism $v:X_u\otimes_\chi A\to X$ whose reduction satisfies $w\circ \bar v=w_u$ on power series. Finally let $O'$ be a local $O^{nr}$-algebra, complete and separated for its maximal ideal, containing $\varpi'\in\mathfrak{m}_{O'}$ with $\varpi'^2$ equal to the image of $q$. Then there exists an $O^{nr}$-algebra homomorphism $\chi:R\to O'$ carrying $\mathfrak{m}_R$ into $\mathfrak{m}_{O'}$. No uniqueness or compatibility with the deformation datum is asserted.
--
--   This is the lifting step in Drinfeld's theory of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules: the universal deformation of $X_0$ acquires a local point over any complete local $O^{nr}$-algebra in which $q$ has a square root in the maximal ideal, so that $X_0$ lifts, with its $\mathcal{O}_D$-action, to a possibly ramified characteristic-zero base. It feeds the construction of fake elliptic curves with prescribed reduction, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_isPullback_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_charZero_of_isAlgClosed_one_of_charP_of_eq_or_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_isPullback_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_charZero_of_isAlgClosed_one_of_charP_of_eq_or_eq).
